# Chapter 11, part 3: spell check and thesaurus, equations, and what the
# programs write at start.
.h2 Spell check and thesaurus [msg-spell]
.ix Messages, Spell check
.ix Messages, Thesaurus
.ix Spell check, messages
.ix Thesaurus, messages
These are the texts of the spell check (Tools, Spell, the key {k:Ctrl-C}) and
of the thesaurus ({k:Ctrl-T}).
{n:spell} describes the commands and {x:spell-messages} gives the
messages in their order of use.
.h3 Boxes [msg-spell-boxes]
.ix Spelling checker not found
.ix Spell, box
.table 18 12 30
Text | Title | Meaning and what to do
A tab or a marker cannot be changed here | Line | The command Line of the
 | | spell check was given a line that has a tab or a marker: that line cannot
 | | be edited in the box.  Use Edit for the word, or correct the text
 | | afterwards.
Cannot make a pipe: REASON | Spell | The program that checks cannot be
 | | connected (no more processes or files).  Try again later.
Cannot start PROGRAM: REASON | Spell | The checker PROGRAM exists and cannot
 | | be run.  Check the program and its rights.
Define: the reason of a failed write | Define | The word cannot be added to
 | | the personal dictionary: the file cannot be written.  The texts are those
 | | of {x:msg-start-config}.
No spelling checker was found.  Install the packages hunspell and
 hunspell-en-us (or aspell and aspell-en); the install script of Strata
 installs them. | Spell | Spell (document, block, section or word) or
 | | {k:Ctrl-C} was used with no checker on the machine.  Install the packages,
 | | or run the install script again.
No spelling checker was found.  Install the packages hunspell and
 hunspell-en-us (or aspell and aspell-en); the install script of Strata
 installs them.  Another program can be named in the variable STRATA_SPELL.
 | Spell | The same, when the spell check is started from the Document
 | | Manager.  The environment variable STRATA_SPELL names a checker
 | | ({n:appcmd-env}).
The spelling checker PROGRAM did not start for the language LANG: its
 dictionary is not installed.  Install the dictionary of that language for
 PROGRAM, or change the Dictionary Language in Setup of the Document Manager.
 | Spell | The same, for a language whose package name is not known: look
 | | for the dictionary of the language in the packages of the checker.
The spelling checker PROGRAM did not start for the language LANG: its
 dictionary is not installed.  Install the package PACKAGE, or change the
 Dictionary Language in Setup of the Document Manager. | Spell | The checker
 | | started and stopped at once: it has no dictionary for LANG. PACKAGE is the
 | | Debian package of that dictionary for that checker, such as hunspell-en-us
 | | or aspell-en.  Install it, or choose another Dictionary Language in Setup.
The spelling checker stopped. | Spell Check, Spell Word | The checker ended in
 | | the middle of a check.  The check is ended; start it again.
There is no word at the cursor | Spell Word | The cursor is on spaces, a
 | | marker, or a place with no letters.  Move onto a word.
.end
.h3 On the check screen and in the word panel [msg-spell-screen]
.ix Check screen, texts
.ix Spelled correctly
.ix Unknown word
These texts are shown on the screen, in the top two rows (the bar) or in the
body.  None of them is an error.
.table 26 34
Text | Where and meaning
Accept correction?  Yes No | The bar, when the only suggestion differs from the
 | word in case only: Yes takes it.
Checking the spelling (Esc quits) | The bar, while the checker works for a
 | long time.
Continue with auto corrections?  Yes No | The bar, after Quit when corrections
 | were made that could be repeated for the rest.
Correct word: | The label of the word in Edit, and of the correction being
 | offered.
Dictionaries: LANG (PROGRAM) | The foot of the screen: the language and the
 | checker, with the file of the personal dictionary on the next line.
Document: NAME | The foot of the screen: the file name, or {c:(not saved)}.
No alternatives found | The bar, when Guess finds no suggestion.
No spelling errors found | The end box: no unknown word was found, or none was
 | changed.
Not found in dictionary | The title of the word panel of Spell Word for a word
 | that is not in the dictionary.
Press any key to exit | The last line of the end box.
Section: Body | The foot of the screen: where the word is ({c:Body (Note)} in
 | a note).
Select word | The bar of suggestions (Guess): choose with the cursor and press
 | {k:Enter}.
Spell Check completed | The end box: the check reached the end.
Spell Check terminated | The end box: the check was ended with Quit.
Spelled correctly | The title of the word panel of Spell Word for a word that
 | is right.
Undo is off: Undo Levels is 0 | Undo or Redo when the setting Undo Levels is
 | 0 ({n:edit-b-undo}).
Undone: and Redone: | The name of the operation that Undo or Redo made, such as
 | "Undone: Paste".
Unknown word: | The label of the word that is not in any dictionary.
Word is too long - maximum length is 65 characters | The title of the word
 | panel of Spell Word, when the word has more than 65 letters.  It is not
 | checked.
.end
.h3 Thesaurus [msg-thesaurus]
.ix Thesaurus not installed
.ix No word selected
.ix Please choose another word
.table 23 12 25
Text | Title | Meaning and what to do
No word selected | Thesaurus | There is no word before the cursor on its line.
 | | Move to a word.
The thesaurus is not installed.  Install the package mythes-en-us; the install
 script of Strata installs it. | Thesaurus | The data of the thesaurus is not
 | | found.  Install the package, or run the install script again.
{c:The word has no synonyms - Please choose another word} | the title of the panel
 | | The word is in the thesaurus but has only generic or related terms,
 | | which are not shown.  Type another in the Look Up box.
{c:The word was not found - Please choose another word} | the title of the panel
 | | The word is not in the thesaurus.  Type another in the Look Up box (the
 | | box opens when a letter is typed).
.end
.h2 Equations [msg-eq]
.ix Messages, equations
.ix Equation, messages
The equation viewer ({k:Ctrl-W}) and the screen show the result of a LaTeX run
on the equation.  An equation that fails keeps its label in the text.  The
messages are listed with their causes in {x:eq-messages}; for the lookup:
.table 33 27
Message | Meaning
Cannot start latex | The program could not be started (no process).  Try again.
dvipng did not make an image | LaTeX made the page and dvipng gave no picture.
latex could not typeset the equation: | A line in the equation viewer, over
 | the message of TeX that follows.
latex took more than 5 seconds | LaTeX ran for more than 5 seconds and was stopped.
No temporary directory for latex | The working directory of the job could
 | not be made.
That TeX command is not allowed in an equation | The text has a refused
 | command ({n:eq-refused}); LaTeX was not run.
The equation did not typeset | LaTeX ended with an error and the log has no
 | line that begins with an exclamation mark.
The equation is empty | The text is only spaces and line ends.
the first lines of the log of LaTeX | The first line that begins with an
 | exclamation mark and up to three after it ({n:msg-other-latex}).
The picture is too large or has no | The picture that LaTeX made is
 size | refused, as is one with more than eight million
 | dots, a cut off or damaged one, or an
 | interlaced one; the message shows which.
Typesetting... | The equation viewer while the job runs.
.end
.h2 What the programs write at start [msg-start]
.ix Messages, start
.ix Interactive terminal, needed
.ix Standard error, start messages
These are the messages of a program that cannot begin, written on the standard
error.
.table 33 27
Message | Meaning and what to do
<Document Manager> needs an interactive terminal (or an X display with the x11
 build) | There is no terminal and no display.  Start it in a terminal.
<Editor> needs an interactive terminal (or an X display with the x11 build)
 | The same.
FILE: cannot open file | The document is not a file or
 | cannot be opened.
FILE: damaged document: a piece of text has no end | The file is damaged: it
 is cut short.
FILE: read error | The file could not be read through.
FILE: The file is not a document of this software. | The file is a text file
 or another kind of file.
FILE: The file is version N.  This software reads up to version 3. | The file
 was written by a newer version of the software.
FILE: The file version is N.  This software reads versions 2 to 3. | The
 version of the file is below the oldest that is read, or it is damaged.
.end
.table 26 34
Message | Meaning
latex: out of memory | Memory ran out while the document was prepared for
 | typesetting.
out of memory | The program ran out of memory while reading a document.
too many markers | The document has more markers than the program can hold.
.end
.h3 Settings and the files of the user [msg-start-config]
.ix Settings, write messages
.ix Config file, messages
The file of settings, the list of fonts and the personal dictionary are written
the same way ({n:appcfg-write-errors}).  The two ways have one different
wording: the settings (Setup, Options) say that a directory is not yours in the
form {c:DIR is not a directory of yours}, and the writes of the other files say
{c:Not a directory of yours: DIR}.
.table 33 27
Message | Meaning
Cannot make DIR: REASON | The directory of the settings cannot be made.
Cannot write FILE: REASON | The file cannot be written.
DIR is not a directory of yours | The directory is a link, a file, or belongs
 | to another user (the settings).
Not a directory of yours: DIR | The same, in the form of the list of fonts and
 | the dictionary.
There is no home directory | No STRATA_HOME and no HOME.
.end
